{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0298","billNumberShort":"H.B. 298","billNumberLong":"HB0298","fileNumber":"2026FL0551","shortTitle":"School Design Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"CHRISKJ","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Christofferson, Kay J.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"","floorSponsorName":"","floorSponsorHouse":"","generalProvisions":"This bill requires the State Board of Education (state board) to establish a library of school building designs.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>establishes a school building design library maintained by the state board;<hr><ltbullet>requires the state board to develop standard designs for elementary, middle, high, and multi-level schools;<hr><ltbullet>requires school districts to own and submit building designs developed using public funds;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes school districts and charter schools to select designs from the library;<hr><ltbullet>establishes periodic review and update requirements for the design library;<hr><ltbullet>requires competitive bidding for architectural and engineering design fees;<hr><ltbullet>mandates life-cycle cost analysis in building designs;<hr><ltbullet>establishes public cost reporting and transparency requirements for school construction projects;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes design-build as an alternative project delivery method; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Jeff Van Hulten","fiscalAnalyst":"Rachelle Gunderson","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"OEWQOHARKY","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-20 15:30:20.440","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description"